WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.410
Heavy rainfall in Nepal can cause rivers
in India to rise thousands of kilometres

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.120
downstream.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:06.310
Look at the map.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.440
Many rivers originating in the
Himalayas flow from Nepal into India.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.490
The Kosi, Gandak and Karnali
are important examples.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.680
During intense monsoon rainfall,

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:18.620
these rivers can carry enormous
amounts of water downstream.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.950
If their water levels rise rapidly,

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.150
communities in northern India
can face serious flooding.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.080
That's why floods aren't always
limited by international borders.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.460
What happens upstream can
directly affect people downstream.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.650
Should India and Nepal
manage their rivers together?

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:34.560
What do you think?

